<title>POLAND: Zasada likely to buy Polish Star issue.</title>
<headline>Zasada likely to buy Polish Star issue.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders of Polish truck maker Star SA will probably sell a three million new share issue to automotive group Sobieslaw Zasada Centrum SA on June 30, Star's president said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Most likely Zasada will take Star's shares... no formal procedures stand in the way of Zasada taking the shares on June 30,&quot; Roman Musial told Reuters.</p>
<p>Musial added that on Friday Star's shareholders did not approve a 3.6 million new shares issue for a consortium led by Polski Bank Rozwoju SA (PBR), opening the door for Zasada, which already has a 28 percent stake in the truck firm.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
